codex
The patch introduces several functional issues in the new busy-session controls, including a no-op Discord implementation, destructive Slack cleanup, media loss on Steer, and incomplete stop/turn-boundary cleanup.

Full review comments:

- [P2] Force-clear sessions for stop-phrase halts — /Users/wondermonkey/.hermes/hermes-agent-buttons/gateway/run.py:2320-2322
  When a user sends a plain stop phrase while the agent is stuck in a tool or still represented by the pending sentinel, this path only calls `running_agent.interrupt(None)` and then returns handled. Unlike `/stop` and the Stop button, it never invalidates/releases the running slot or clears adapter session activity, so the chat can remain locked even though the user gets a 🙊 acknowledgement.

- [P2] Keep media queued when Steer only sends text — /Users/wondermonkey/.hermes/hermes-agent-buttons/gateway/run.py:2474-2478
  If a busy follow-up contains media with a caption and the user taps Steer, only `joined_text` is injected via `running_agent.steer(...)`; this branch then removes the queued event, so the image/document URLs are silently discarded and never reach the next turn. Since steer is text-only, media-bearing follow-ups should stay queued or make the steer action fail without popping the pending message.

- [P1] Preserve Slack messages when clearing busy buttons — /Users/wondermonkey/.hermes/hermes-agent-buttons/gateway/platforms/slack.py:3073-3082
  When the runner clears each busy-button anchor, this Slack implementation ignores the `message_id` it was asked to clear, pops the single stored mapping, and updates that stored message with `blocks=[]` and `text=""`. On Slack busy-button cleanup this can blank the ack/tool message that held the latest mapping, while older anchors keep stale active buttons because subsequent calls no longer have coords.

- [P2] Move Discord busy controls onto DiscordAdapter — /Users/wondermonkey/.hermes/hermes-agent-buttons/gateway/platforms/discord.py:4786-4790
  These intended adapter overrides are defined in the module-level `if DISCORD_AVAILABLE:` block after `DiscordAdapter` has already ended, not on `DiscordAdapter` itself. As a result Discord instances still inherit the no-op `BasePlatformAdapter.attach_busy_session_buttons`/clear/reaction methods, so the new busy buttons never render or dispatch on Discord.

- [P2] Clear follow-up button state before queued turns — /Users/wondermonkey/.hermes/hermes-agent-buttons/gateway/run.py:13990-13991
  In queue mode, a pending follow-up is processed via `return await self._run_agent(...)` before this `finally` cleanup runs, so `_pending_followups` from the previous turn remains populated while that queued turn is executing. If the user sends another busy follow-up and taps a button during the queued turn, the button handler joins the old already-consumed prompt with the new text, causing duplicate/incorrect steer or interrupt input.
The patch introduces several functional issues in the new busy-session controls, including a no-op Discord implementation, destructive Slack cleanup, media loss on Steer, and incomplete stop/turn-boundary cleanup.

Full review comments:

- [P2] Force-clear sessions for stop-phrase halts — /Users/wondermonkey/.hermes/hermes-agent-buttons/gateway/run.py:2320-2322
  When a user sends a plain stop phrase while the agent is stuck in a tool or still represented by the pending sentinel, this path only calls `running_agent.interrupt(None)` and then returns handled. Unlike `/stop` and the Stop button, it never invalidates/releases the running slot or clears adapter session activity, so the chat can remain locked even though the user gets a 🙊 acknowledgement.

- [P2] Keep media queued when Steer only sends text — /Users/wondermonkey/.hermes/hermes-agent-buttons/gateway/run.py:2474-2478
  If a busy follow-up contains media with a caption and the user taps Steer, only `joined_text` is injected via `running_agent.steer(...)`; this branch then removes the queued event, so the image/document URLs are silently discarded and never reach the next turn. Since steer is text-only, media-bearing follow-ups should stay queued or make the steer action fail without popping the pending message.

- [P1] Preserve Slack messages when clearing busy buttons — /Users/wondermonkey/.hermes/hermes-agent-buttons/gateway/platforms/slack.py:3073-3082
  When the runner clears each busy-button anchor, this Slack implementation ignores the `message_id` it was asked to clear, pops the single stored mapping, and updates that stored message with `blocks=[]` and `text=""`. On Slack busy-button cleanup this can blank the ack/tool message that held the latest mapping, while older anchors keep stale active buttons because subsequent calls no longer have coords.

- [P2] Move Discord busy controls onto DiscordAdapter — /Users/wondermonkey/.hermes/hermes-agent-buttons/gateway/platforms/discord.py:4786-4790
  These intended adapter overrides are defined in the module-level `if DISCORD_AVAILABLE:` block after `DiscordAdapter` has already ended, not on `DiscordAdapter` itself. As a result Discord instances still inherit the no-op `BasePlatformAdapter.attach_busy_session_buttons`/clear/reaction methods, so the new busy buttons never render or dispatch on Discord.

- [P2] Clear follow-up button state before queued turns — /Users/wondermonkey/.hermes/hermes-agent-buttons/gateway/run.py:13990-13991
  In queue mode, a pending follow-up is processed via `return await self._run_agent(...)` before this `finally` cleanup runs, so `_pending_followups` from the previous turn remains populated while that queued turn is executing. If the user sends another busy follow-up and taps a button during the queued turn, the button handler joins the old already-consumed prompt with the new text, causing duplicate/incorrect steer or interrupt input.
